## Completion evidence — 2026-10-15

Implemented the public "'`/ralph-commands` router/plugin boundary, bundled read-only
command discovery, strict lifecycle schema/platform coverage, exact revision/hash
approval correlation, atomic command save, immutable approved revision archives,
verification status/readiness assertion, per-command host permissions, environment
references/redaction, bounded logs, owned process wrappers, timeouts/readiness and
cleanup of partial startup. Save intent with approval request/session/message identity
and verification results use the predecessor RunStore. Replacement rejection or stale
approval preserves the previously verified file. Setup is serialized across linked
worktrees; cwd symlink escapes are rejected at execution.

TDD red/green evidence: first rejection test failed because `setupProject` did not exist;
it passed after adding proposal/approval handling. Approved verification initially
returned `not-ready` and became green after lifecycle execution. The HTTP/argv/secret
fixture exposed Bun'"'s missing IPC-channel "'`unref` method and canonical macOS temp-path
behavior; corrected implementation/test expectations made it green. An overlapping
setup test demonstrated a second configuration executing during pending approval;
the repository lock made it green. The immutable archive assertion failed with ENOENT
before archive storage and passed afterward. Additional failure/denial/schema/cleanup
regressions exercise already implemented behavior through public interfaces.

Validation on macOS arm64/Bun 1.4.3: `bun run typecheck` passed. The slice'"'s
"'`bun test tests/integration/02-project-commands.test.ts` has 15 passing tests.
`bun test --timeout 30000 tests/integration` passed 90 tests, skipped 1 gated browser
probe, failed 0 (before the final archive assertion and registered-command test were
added; the final slice suite was rerun afterward). Predecessor suite alone passed 19.
Biome passes all 11 changed source/test files. Repository-wide `bun run lint` fails
only on formatting in untouched `tests/browser/dashboard.test.ts:38`; it was not edited
because this task prohibits unrelated changes.

Demonstration: the public `dispatch("ralph-commands", ..., mainSession)` boundary
uses fake SDK repository discovery and a correlated host human approval. The portable
fixture executes setup/check with unchanged space-containing arguments and referenced
environment values, starts an HTTP service plus descendant, verifies the HTTP endpoint,
cleans the tree, and inspects verified status, saved JSON, and its immutable archive.
A failing check returns not-ready with phase/exit/log evidence and still runs cleanup;
cleanup failure also blocks `assertProjectReady`. No application credentials are used.

**Remaining blocker; this ticket is not fully complete:** the predecessor'"'s pinned v2
adapter explicitly lacks verified human-input provenance. Production "'`requestUserInput`
continues returning unsupported; neither assistant/API-created messages nor permission
replies are substituted for human approval. A registered-command fixture proves this
stops before writing commands. The host'"'s real "'`ctx.permission.assert` is wired for
execution authorization, but live approval/permission interaction was not smoke-tested.
Native Linux/Windows execution remains unrun locally; platform coverage is explicit in
config and the runner includes Windows argument-array/tree-cleanup paths. Interrupted
setup locks remain retained and require reconciliation rather than automatic stealing.

Wiki created: `docs/wiki/features/project-commands.md`; index/open questions and
README/compatibility limitations updated. No publication, external message or branch
merge was performed.
